{
  "task": "Write Python 3 function solve(rows). First apply an audit filter to the ORIGINAL input positions, indexed from zero: omit positions whose index modulo 4 equals 1, except always retain the last input position. Rotate the retained rows LEFT by 3 positions modulo the retained length (empty stays empty). Apply the following rules to that transformed list: Rows [kind,value] update a running balance starting at zero. add increases it, reset replaces it. After EACH row clamp balance to [-11,11]. Return every resulting balance.\nReturn the requested value, without printing. Inputs follow the types specified. Do not mutate the input. Standard library is allowed.",
  "specification": "First apply an audit filter to the ORIGINAL input positions, indexed from zero: omit positions whose index modulo 4 equals 1, except always retain the last input position. Rotate the retained rows LEFT by 3 positions modulo the retained length (empty stays empty). Apply the following rules to that transformed list: Rows [kind,value] update a running balance starting at zero. add increases it, reset replaces it. After EACH row clamp balance to [-11,11]. Return every resulting balance.",
  "reference": "def solve(rows):\n x=0; out=[]\n for kind,v in rows:\n  x=v if kind=='reset' else x+v\n  x=max(-11,min(11,x))\n  out.append(x)\n return out\n_core_solve=solve\ndef solve(rows):\n filtered=[row for i,row in enumerate(rows) if i%4!=1 or i==len(rows)-1]\n if filtered:\n  shift=3%len(filtered)\n  filtered=filtered[shift:]+filtered[:shift]\n return _core_solve(filtered)",
  "mutation": "def solve(rows):\n x=0; out=[]\n for kind,v in rows:\n  x=v if kind=='reset' else x+v\n  x=max(0,min(11,x))\n  out.append(x)\n return out\n_core_solve=solve\ndef solve(rows):\n filtered=[row for i,row in enumerate(rows) if i%4!=1 or i==len(rows)-1]\n if filtered:\n  shift=3%len(filtered)\n  filtered=filtered[shift:]+filtered[:shift]\n return _core_solve(filtered)",
